            "name": "submit_note",
            "input": {
              "body": "Corella Fresh Foods is in breach of the net leverage covenant for the test period ending 30 September 2026. Interest cover and minimum liquidity pass but are on watch.\n\nNet leverage: tested 3.82x against a maximum of 3.50x, a breach with headroom of -9.1%. The certificate reports 3.39x and compliance. The difference is EBITDA. The certificate uses 5,300, which adds back flood-related spoilage ($420k) and Gatton restructuring ($180k) to the P&L figure. The P&L TTM EBITDA is 4,700, and the covenant uses the P&L figure. The certificate's compliance statement and \"no Default is continuing\" do not hold on the tested figures.\n\nInterest cover: tested 2.35x against a minimum of 2.25x, headroom 4.4%, watch. The certificate reports 2.65x, which uses the adjusted EBITDA.\n\nMinimum liquidity: 3,250k (cash 1,250k plus undrawn revolver 2,000k) against a minimum of 3,000k, headroom 8.3%, watch. The certificate agrees.\n\nReview issues:\n- Certificate EBITDA adds back $600k not shown in the P&L (page 6).\n- Cash at bank fell 33% from $1,870k to $1,250k in the quarter (page 4).\n- The pack notes a further $300k revolver draw in late September, and $510k of spoilage was restated after the 9 October pack.\n\nRecommended action: Analyst to treat net leverage as a breach pending the borrower's response. Request a reconciliation of the certificate to the P&L, and confirm whether a Default has occurred and what notice has been given. Consider reservation of rights and waiver discussions, and monitor liquidity closely given the revolver draw."
            },
