            "type": "text",
            "text": "The September 2026 monitoring run for Corella Fresh Foods is complete, and the note is saved for analyst sign-off.\n\n**Covenant results (tested from the pack):**\n\n| Covenant | Tested | Limit | Headroom | Status | Certificate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Net leverage | 3.82x | max 3.50x | -9.1% | **Breach** | 3.39x, \"Complies\" |\n| Interest cover | 2.35x | min 2.25x | 4.4% | Watch | 2.65x, \"Complies\" |\n| Minimum liquidity | $3,250k | min $3,000k | 8.3% | Watch | $3,250k, \"Complies\" |\n\nThe certificate's net leverage and interest cover figures use EBITDA of $5,300k. That adds back $600k of flood spoilage and Gatton restructuring costs that the P&L does not show. The covenant uses the P&L TTM EBITDA of $4,700k, which gives the breach.\n\n**Figures submitted:** All six required figures were accepted on the first attempt. Revenue TTM is $59,840k, EBITDA TTM $4,700k, interest TTM $2,000k, total drawn debt $19,200k, cash $1,250k and undrawn revolver $2,000k. Leases are excluded from debt, as the facility requires.\n\n**Review issues flagged:**\n- The certificate adds back $600k that is not in the P&L.\n- Cash fell 33% in the quarter, from $1,870k to $1,250k.\n\n**Recommended action in the note:** Treat net leverage as a breach pending the borrower's response. Ask for a reconciliation of the certificate to the P&L and confirm whether a Default has occurred. Consider a reservation of rights and waiver discussions, and monitor liquidity given the $300k revolver draw in late September.\n\nThe first version of the note was 246 words, over the 220-word limit, so I shortened it before saving."
